<newsitem itemid="414301" id="root" date="1997-03-03" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa Educor year share jumps.</title>
<headline>S.Africa Educor year share jumps.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     8.2	   vs 3.2</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 4.0	   vs 1.6</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   18.89	 vs 6.97</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   27.91	 vs 11.39</p>
<p>    Tax			 7.50	  vs 4.42</p>
<p>    Interest received     3.41	  vs 0.41</p>
<p>    Turnover		  127.0	 vs 80.58</p>
<p>Full name: Education Investment Corp Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The comparative figures are pro-forma.</p>
<p>The firm said that it had decided to award capitalisation shares to ordinary shareholders registered on March 20.</p>
<p>It added market conditions had created an environment conducive to continued strong earnings growth. It added that it would be opening several new campuses in 1997 with other venues on track for 1998.</p>
<p>Educor said it expected additional growth from pursuing a selective acquisition policy.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
